## What happened along the way
- **`main` had moved.** It now includes commit `066253a`, which changes `groupThousands` to `toLocaleString("en-US")`, and it was not an ancestor of the head. I merged it in as `60d5644` before `GC baseline`.
- **QA carries and re-runs.** That merge only changes how totals of 1000 or more are formatted:
  - The four F1 checks with totals under 1000 (s1–s4) are carried and were not re-run.
  - The large-total check (s5) was stale: the F1 capture showed `1234.50`. I re-ran it on the merged head and it now prints `1,234.50`, which the expectation in tasks.md 3.1 allows.
  - I also captured the spec's `0.10 + 0.20 → 0.30` scenario, which F1 had not captured, so the "exact cents" row covers all its scenarios.
- **Record fix.** The first validation failed with `blockers: must be an array`. I added `"blockers": []`, re-staged, and it passed.
- **Checkout changed.** The skill requires reviewing from a dedicated worktree, so I switched the main checkout (clean: no changes, no untracked files, no stashes) to `main`. `feat/csv-total` is now checked out in the locked worktree `.worktrees/review-csv-total`. That worktree also holds the gate ledger and snapshot (git-ignored).

